sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2025-wisdom-03> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Levin defines intelligence, following William James, as the ability to reach the same goal by different means; for tissues this is the problem-solving competency to adapt to conditions in order to construct and repair a specific morphology or function, a functional definition that lets intelligence be studied in non-neural substrates.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Intelligence is reaching the same goal by different means, including in morphogenesis";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “The Multiscale Wisdom of the Body: Collective Intelligence as a Tractable Interface for Next-Generation Biomedicine”, BioEssays : news and reviews in molecular, cellular and developmental biology (2025), doi:10.1002/bies.202400196; section “Intelligence Below the Cellular Level”. Scope: Any biological system, from molecular networks to organisms"
}
